# Luttwak Primary Source Extracts
## Source: The Grand Strategy of the Byzantine Empire (Harvard UP, 2009)
## Date: 2026-06-06

See `/root/work/method-sourcing-board/luttwak-primary-extracts.md` for full verified extracts.

Key verified passages:
- Strategy defined: "the level at which knowledge and persuasion, or in modern terms intelligence and diplomacy, interact with military strength"
- Paradoxical logic: "the straightest and broadest and best-paved highway is the worst road upon which to attack an enemy"
- Operational Code: 7 principles (avoid war, gather intelligence, campaign with small units, maneuver over attrition, recruit allies, subversion, relational methods)
- Strategy as culture: "it is always the expression of an entire culture"
- Military subordinated to diplomacy in Byzantine scheme
